Description: btattach from bluez 5.87 source (UART H4 attach workaround)
 Workaround for a btattach regression in resolute (26.04) bluez 5.85:
 the -S baud rate value is OR'd raw into termios c_cflag, so the speed
 field reads B0 (hangup), RTS gets deasserted and CTS-gated H4
 controllers never attach. All standard baud rates are even numbers,
 the low speed bits are therefore always zero - there is no
 argument-level workaround.
 .
 This package builds btattach from the bluez 5.87 release source
 (with the upstream glibc 2.42 fix) and installs it as /usr/bin/btattach
 via dpkg-divert; the distro binary is kept at /usr/bin/btattach.distrib
 and restored automatically when this package is removed.
 .
 Remove this package once the distribution ships a fixed btattach.

